  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{4x}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{5}{4x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934099/assets/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{5}{4}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{4x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934099/assets/6e56262645ef598cacb1377193398f1f3a59a2637193d05c813ffa075603c262.png)",
